# cluster.env — per-user config for the `cluster` helper (SLURM from inside the
# yolo container). COPY this to your private config; do NOT commit your filled-in
# copy. It is personal to you and your account:
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/yolo
#   cp cluster.env.example ~/.config/yolo/cluster.env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/yolo/cluster.env
#
# bin/yolo sources ~/.config/yolo/cluster.env at launch and forwards these into
# the container, where `cluster` uses them to ssh to your login node and run
# slurm there.
#
# TWO ways to supply the SSH identity — pick one:
#   A. Server-resident keyfile (YOLO_SLURM_KEYFILE) — PREFERRED. A passphrase-less
#      key that lives on the cluster, so `cluster` and `git push` keep working even
#      when your laptop (and its forwarded ssh-agent) is detached. See README →
#      "Server-resident SSH key" for how to generate and register it.
#   B. Forwarded ssh-agent (YOLO_SLURM_KEY) — fallback for the connected case. Your
#      SSH key never leaves the agent; we only name which loaded key to use. Dies
#      when the laptop leaves.
# If both are set, the keyfile wins.

# Login / submit host — where sbatch, squeue, sacct live.
YOLO_SLURM_LOGIN=slurm.bgu.ac.il

# Your username on the cluster. REQUIRED: the container runs as uid 0, so without
# this ssh would try to log in as root@ and fail.
YOLO_SLURM_USER=your_username

# (A, preferred) HOST path to the server-resident private key. bin/yolo mounts it
# read-only into the container and points `cluster` + git at it. Generate it ON
# the cluster (passphrase-less), authorize its .pub in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys and
# on GitHub — see README → "Server-resident SSH key".
# YOLO_SLURM_KEYFILE=~/.ssh/yolo_server

# (B, fallback) Which key in your forwarded agent authenticates to the login node.
# Run `ssh-add -l` and copy the trailing comment of the right key, EXACTLY. Pinning
# one key avoids "Too many authentication failures" when the agent holds several.
# QUOTE it — key comments usually contain spaces, and this file is shell-sourced.
# Ignored when YOLO_SLURM_KEYFILE is set.
YOLO_SLURM_KEY="my cluster key"

# (optional) Container mount point that maps to your project. Default /workspace;
# leave commented unless you've customized bin/yolo's workspace mount.
# YOLO_WS_CONTAINER=/workspace
